.TH NETPIPE 1 "June 2026" "netpipe v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netpipe \- modular network traffic stream-processing engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netpipe
[
.I OPTIONS
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netpipe
is a high-performance command-line network packet processing tool that operates as a
composable, modular stream processor.
It captures packets from network interfaces or reads them from files,
applies filters and processors, and routes them to one or more output sinks.
.PP
Key capabilities include TCP stream reassembly (out-of-order, retransmission,
gap-fill), TLS 1.2/1.3 session decryption via NSS key-log files, inline Lua
scripting for custom packet processing, and a token-bucket rate limiter.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input Options
.TP
.BI \-i " device"
Perform live capture on the specified network interface (e.g., eth0, wlo1, any).
Requires root privileges or the
.B CAP_NET_RAW
capability.
.TP
.BI \-r " file.pcap"
Read packets from the specified PCAP or PCAP-NG file.
Does not require root privileges.
.TP
.B \-D
List all available capture devices and exit.
.TP
.BI \-s " snaplen"
Set the maximum bytes captured per packet.
Default is 65535 (full packet).
.TP
.B \-p
Disable promiscuous mode.
By default, live captures put the network card into promiscuous mode.
.TP
.BI \-T " ms"
Set the read timeout for live captures in milliseconds.
Default is 1000 ms.
.TP
.B \-\-ring
Use a high-performance zero-copy
.B AF_PACKET + PACKET_MMAP
ring-buffer source instead of libpcap (Linux only).
Requires an interface specified with
.BR \-i .
Requires root or
.BR CAP_NET_RAW .
.SS Filtering Options
Multiple filters are logically ANDed.
.TP
.BI \-f " bpf-expr"
Specify a Berkeley Packet Filter (BPF) expression
(e.g.,
.IR "tcp port 443" ,
.IR icmp ).
.TP
.BI \-proto " name"
Match packets containing the named protocol in their layer stack.
Supported names:
.IR eth ,
.IR arp ,
.IR ip ,
.IR ip6 ,
.IR icmp ,
.IR tcp ,
.IR udp ,
.IR dns ,
.IR http ,
.IR tls ,
.IR quic ,
.IR dhcp ,
.IR sip ,
.IR mqtt ,
.IR vxlan .
.TP
.BI \-port " number"
Match packets whose source or destination port equals
.IR number .
.TP
.BI \-host " ip"
Match packets whose source or destination IPv4 address equals
.IR ip .
.SS Processing Options
.TP
.BI \-proc " spec"
Attach a built-in processor.
.I spec
is one of:
.RS
.IP "tcp-stream" 14
Reassemble TCP byte-streams with out-of-order segment buffering,
retransmission detection, hole-timeout gap flushing, and SYN/FIN/RST
state machine.
Populates the
.B stream_data
/
.B stream_len
fields on each packet.
.IP "flow-tracker" 14
Associate packets with bidirectional flows by five-tuple hash.
Includes automatic GC of idle flows (60s timeout).
.IP "rate-limit:\fIN\fP" 14
Token-bucket rate limiter; allow at most
.I N
bytes per second through the pipeline.
Uses
.BR nanosleep (2)
for high-resolution timing.
.IP "transform:\fImode\fP:\fIpattern\fP:\fIreplacement\fP" 14
Search-and-replace payload bytes.
.I mode
is
.B literal
or
.BR regex .
.IP "lua:\fIscript.lua\fP" 14
Execute the Lua script for every packet.
The script can register
.BR init (),
.BR process (pkt),
and
.BR free ()
callbacks.
Returning
.B false
from
.B process()
drops the packet from the pipeline.
.IP "tls-decrypt:\fIkeylog.txt\fP" 14
Decrypt TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 traffic inline using an NSS key-log file
.RB ( SSLKEYLOGFILE
format).
Supports AES-128-GCM, AES-256-GCM, and ChaCha20-Poly1305 cipher suites.
Decrypted plaintext is placed in
.B stream_data
and the TLS layer's
.B data
pointer is redirected to the plaintext.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-rate " bps"
Rate-limit output to
.I bps
bytes per second (shorthand for
.BR \-proc " rate-limit:\fIbps\fP" ).
.SS Output Options
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write packet data to
.IR file .
If the output format is not specified with
.BR \-fmt ,
the format is inferred from the file extension
(.pcap, .pcapng, .json, .hex, .stats).
Use \- to write to standard output.
Special schemes:
.RS
.IP "tap://\fIdev\fP" 18
Inject packets into a Linux TAP (Layer 2) virtual interface.
Requires root or
.BR CAP_NET_ADMIN .
.IP "tun://\fIdev\fP" 18
Inject packets into a Linux TUN (Layer 3) virtual interface.
Requires root or
.BR CAP_NET_ADMIN .
.IP "socket://\fIhost:port\fP" 18
Forward raw PCAP stream to a remote host over TCP.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-fmt " format"
Force the output format, overriding extension inference.
Supported formats:
.RS
.IP "pcap" 10
Wireshark-compatible binary PCAP (libpcap format).
.IP "pcapng" 10
PCAP-NG with interface-description and metadata blocks.
.IP "json" 10
Newline-delimited JSON (NDJSON), one object per packet.
See
.BR netpipe-python (7)
for the JSON schema.
.IP "hex" 10
Human-readable annotated hex dump with layer boundaries.
.IP "stats" 10
Periodic summary of packet and byte counters (every 5 seconds).
.IP "pretty" 10
tshark-style single-line packet summaries.
.IP "null" 10
Discard packets (useful with processors or
.BR \-stats ).
.RE
.TP
.BI \-stats " file"
Write a periodic statistics report to
.I file
(use \- for stdout) every 5 seconds independently of the main output sink.
.TP
.BI \-c " count"
Terminate the pipeline after processing
.I count
packets.
.SS Logging Options
.TP
.B \-v
Enable verbose (DEBUG-level) logs.
.TP
.B \-vv
Enable trace-level logs (very noisy; useful for debugging the demuxer).
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode; only warnings and errors are logged.
.TP
.B \-no-color
Disable ANSI color escape sequences in log output.
.SS Miscellaneous Options
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH TLS DECRYPTION
.B netpipe
can decrypt TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 traffic inline if an NSS key-log file
.RB ( SSLKEYLOGFILE
format) is provided.
The key-log file is emitted by Chrome, Firefox, curl, OpenSSL, and other
TLS implementations when the
.B SSLKEYLOGFILE
environment variable is set.
.PP
Supported cipher suites:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 3
TLS 1.3:
.IR TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256
.IP \(bu 3
TLS 1.2 (GCM/ChaCha20):
.IR ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 ,
.IR ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256
.RE
.PP
Supported key-log record types:
.IR CLIENT_RANDOM ,
.IR CLIENT_HANDSHAKE_TRAFFIC_SECRET ,
.IR SERVER_HANDSHAKE_TRAFFIC_SECRET ,
.IR CLIENT_TRAFFIC_SECRET_0 ,
.IR SERVER_TRAFFIC_SECRET_0 .
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
.RS
SSLKEYLOGFILE=/tmp/keys.log curl https://example.com &
netpipe \-i eth0 \-f "tcp port 443" \\
        \-proc tls\-decrypt:/tmp/keys.log \\
        \-fmt json
.RE
.fi
.SH LUA SCRIPTING
Lua scripts register a processor via
.BR NP_REGISTER_PROCESSOR(\fItable\fP) .
The table may contain:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 3
.BR init() \(em called once when the processor is created.
.IP \(bu 3
.BR process( pkt ) \(em called for every packet.
Return
.B true
to keep, or
.B false
to drop the packet from downstream sinks.
.IP \(bu 3
.BR free() \(em called once when the processor is freed.
.RE
.PP
The
.I pkt
table exposes fields like
.IR proto ,
.IR src_ip ,
.IR dst_ip ,
.IR src_port ,
.IR dst_port ,
.IR dns_query_name ,
.IR raw_hex ,
and
.IR stream_hex .
.PP
A production-ready DNS IDS script (
.BR mitigate.lua )
is bundled and can be used as:
.PP
.nf
.RS
netpipe \-i eth0 \-proc lua:mitigate.lua \-fmt json
.RE
.fi
.SH RECIPES
.TP
Live capture to PCAP:
.B sudo netpipe \-i eth0 \-o capture.pcap
.TP
Watch HTTP traffic as annotated hex:
.B "sudo netpipe \-i wlo1 \-f \"tcp port 80\" \-fmt hex"
.TP
Readable one-line summaries with
.BR pretty :
.B "sudo netpipe \-i wlo1 \-proto dns \-fmt pretty"
.TP
Extract DNS traffic as JSON (pipe to jq):
.B "sudo netpipe \-i eth0 \-proto dns \-fmt json | jq ."
.TP
Analyse a PCAP file offline:
.B "netpipe \-r capture.pcap \-host 1.2.3.4 \-fmt hex | less"
.TP
Capture 100 packets then stop:
.B sudo netpipe \-i wlo1 \-c 100 \-o top100.pcap
.TP
Live stats to stdout while capturing to file:
.B "sudo netpipe \-i eth0 \-o session.pcap \-stats \-"
.TP
TCP stream reassembly with JSON output:
.B "sudo netpipe \-i wlo1 \-proto http \-proc tcp-stream \-fmt json"
.TP
Zero-copy ring-buffer capture:
.B "sudo netpipe \-i eth0 \-\-ring \-o capture.pcap"
.TP
TLS decryption:
.B "sudo netpipe \-i eth0 \-f \"tcp port 443\" \-proc tls-decrypt:/tmp/keys.log \-fmt json"
.TP
Lua IDS (DNS exfil detection):
.B "sudo netpipe \-i eth0 \-proc lua:mitigate.lua \-fmt null"
.TP
Forward packets to a remote collector:
.B "sudo netpipe \-i eth0 \-c 50 \-o socket://192.168.1.10:9999"
.TP
Inject packets into a TAP interface:
.B "sudo netpipe \-r cap.pcap \-o tap://tap0 \-rate 10000"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Pipeline completed normally (including Ctrl-C / SIGINT).
.TP
.B 1
A configuration or runtime error occurred; details logged to stderr.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/netpipe/lua/mitigate.lua
Bundled DNS IDS Lua script.
.TP
.I /usr/share/netpipe/lua/test.lua
Bundled DNS exfil-payload isolation harness (for testing).
